    <h2>What Is the Royal Oreo® Blizzard® Treat?</h2>
    <p>The Royal Oreo® Blizzard starts with the same foundation as the classic <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo Cookie Blizzard</a> — DQ vanilla soft serve hand-blended with real Oreo cookie pieces throughout. The Royal upgrade injects a warm hot fudge-filled center into the cup before serving. When you reach the middle, the fudge creates a temperature and flavor contrast that makes the Royal version a genuinely different experience, not just a more expensive one.</p>
  <p>Browse the full Blizzard lineup on <a href="/">The Dairy Queen Menu</a> or see all flavors on the <a href="/categories/blizzard-treats">Blizzard Treats</a> category page.</p>

    <h2>Royal vs. Standard Oreo — Is the Upgrade Worth It?</h2>
  <p>The Royal Oreo costs approximately $1 more per size than the <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">standard Oreo Blizzard</a>. Whether the upgrade is worth it depends on what you want from your dessert. If you enjoy the Oreo Blizzard exactly as-is and want the familiar experience, stick with the original. If you want a mid-dessert moment where the flavor changes — where the warm fudge hits differently than the cold soft serve — the Royal Oreo delivers that in a way no other standard Blizzard does.</p>
  <h2>The Four Royal Blizzard Flavors</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/items/royal-oreo-blizzard"><strong>Royal Oreo® Blizzard</strong></a> — Hot fudge center. The most popular Royal flavor.</li>
    <li><a href="/items/royal-reeses-blizzard"><strong>Royal Reese's® Blizzard</strong></a> — Peanut butter center. Second most popular.</li>
    <li><strong>Royal New York Cheesecake Blizzard</strong> — Strawberry center. Graham crackers and cheesecake pieces.</li>
    <li><strong>Royal Rocky Road Trip Blizzard</strong> — Fudge center. Brownie pieces, almonds, marshmallow.</li>
  </ul>

